var e=`# Rule 45: Hauling Out; Making Fast; Anchoring

**Part 4 — Other Requirements When Racing**  
**Section A — General Requirements**

**Source:** Racing Rules of Sailing 2021-2024, World Sailing  
https://www.sailing.org/inside-world-sailing/rules-regulations/racingrules/

---

"A boat shall be afloat and off moorings at her preparatory signal. Thereafter, she shall not be hauled out or made fast except to bail out, reef sails or make repairs." The boat may anchor or crew may stand on the bottom but must recover the anchor before continuing unless unable to do so.
`;export{e as default};